---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const proofBase = '/proofs/vercel-ai-chatbot-mapper';
const artifacts = [
  { label: 'SYSTEM_MAP.md', href: `${proofBase}/SYSTEM_MAP.md`, text: 'Observed frameworks, APIs, integrations, risk zones, and human review questions.' },
  { label: 'BUILDPRINT_CANDIDATES.md', href: `${proofBase}/BUILDPRINT_CANDIDATES.md`, text: 'Five scoped Buildprint candidates found before any final extraction.' },
  { label: 'SELECTED_CANDIDATE.md', href: `${proofBase}/SELECTED_CANDIDATE.md`, text: 'The chosen AI Workflow Buildprint boundary for agent handoff.' },
  { label: 'facts.json', href: `${proofBase}/facts.json`, text: 'Deterministic machine-readable mapper facts.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Vercel AI Chatbot mapper proof — Agent Buildprint" description="A public proof showing Vercel AI Chatbot mapped into scoped Buildprint candidates and a selected AI Workflow Buildprint.">
  <main>
    <section class="container hero detail-hero proof-hero">
      <a class="pill" href="/buildprints/buildprint-mapper-os/">← Buildprint Mapper</a>
      <h1>Vercel AI Chatbot → scoped Buildprint candidates.</h1>
      <p class="lead">A real public repo mapped into Buildprint candidates. The mapper workflow found a complex Next.js + Vercel AI SDK app, produced candidate Buildprints, then selected the AI Workflow candidate for focused agent handoff.</p>
      <div class="tags detail-meta"><span class="tag hot">Proof artifact</span><span class="tag">Next.js</span><span class="tag">Vercel AI SDK</span><span class="tag">Auth + DB/cache</span></div>
      <div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href={`${proofBase}/BUILDPRINT_CANDIDATES.md`}>Open candidates</a><a class="btn" href="https://github.com/vercel/ai-chatbot">Source repo</a><a class="btn" href="/buildprints/buildprint-mapper-os/">Use Buildprint Mapper</a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="container section proof-summary-grid">
      <div class="panel proof-stat"><b>180</b><span>files scanned</span></div>
      <div class="panel proof-stat"><b>4</b><span>UI routes</span></div>
      <div class="panel proof-stat"><b>11</b><span>API routes</span></div>
      <div class="panel proof-stat"><b>5</b><span>candidate Buildprints</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="container section">
      <div class="section-head compact"><div><span class="eyebrow"><b>⌁</b> Selected candidate</span><h2>AI Workflow Buildprint</h2></div></div>
      <div class="grid columns two proof-two">
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>What the mapper selected</h3>
          <p>LLM calls, prompts, tools, model adapters, grounding and safety checks — the slice most likely to become a reusable agent-grade Buildprint.</p>
          <ul class="clean-list check-list">
            <li>Detected Vercel AI SDK integration</li>
            <li>Separated AI workflow from auth/session and generic route/API candidates</li>
            <li>Listed included paths before implementation handoff</li>
            <li>Preserved questions instead of inventing model/provider intent</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="panel command-card">
          <div class="panel-row"><span class="eyebrow"><b>◆</b> Workflow</span></div>
          <code class="command-line">SYSTEM_MAP.md → BUILDPRINT_CANDIDATES.md → SELECTED_CANDIDATE.md</code>
          <p>Candidate selection creates a focused handoff so the next coding agent stays inside the selected boundary instead of flattening the whole repo.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="container section">
      <div class="section-head compact"><div><span class="eyebrow"><b>↳</b> Artifacts</span><h2>Open the proof files</h2></div></div>
      <div class="grid mapper-output-grid">
        {artifacts.map((artifact) => <a class="panel mapper-artifact proof-artifact-link" href={artifact.href}><code>{artifact.label}</code><h3>{artifact.label.replace(/\.(md|json)$/,'')}</h3><p>{artifact.text}</p></a>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="container section">
      <div class="panel proof-note">
        <span class="eyebrow"><b>!</b> Honest boundary</span>
        <h2>This is mapper proof, not a full app audit.</h2>
        <p>The mapper produced deterministic facts and scoped candidates. Business intent, provider choices, and final validation still require human review before treating the selected candidate as publishable architecture truth.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
